  "id": "Compound::DB00290 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hematologic Cancer through a series of interconnected mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Bleomycin causes Skin Toxicity, which is mediated by Imatinib, a drug that treats Hematologic Cancer. This creates a chain of causation where Bleomycin's effects are linked to Imatinib's therapeutic action. The shared lowest common ancestors—Organic Amino Compound and Antineoplastic Agent—highlight a common biological function across these entities, reinforcing the notion of a broader pharmacological relationship. Additionally, Bleomycin's role in causing Cerebral Arteritis, mediated by Cisplatin, which in turn treats Hematologic Cancer, further supports the idea that Bleomycin may have a broader impact on cancer treatment through different pathways. These findings suggest that Bleomycin may contribute to the treatment of Hematologic Cancer through its ability to induce toxicity that is mitigated by Imatinib or other antineoplastic agents, thereby supporting a potential repositioning of Bleomycin in cancer therapy.",
